  "notes": "Bubblegum dance-pop idol group (\"color pop\") migrating through tropical house, city-pop and disco, flagged as a K-pop sub-lane. The class is straight throughout. The kit folds the entry's three modes: \"teen-pop kick/clap with 16th hats; the tropical-house material uses offbeat shakers and a pitched pluck instead of hats; the new-jack-swing-facing tracks use a swung, ghost-noted snare.\" The new-jack half is the only place this model swings — `swing.amount` 0.56 on a 16th grid with a dense ghost map — while the tropical half is the `shaker` lane at `offbeat` placement and a high `openHat.prob` on the offbeats. No `bass808` block: \"no 808 idiom in the core mode — synth bass on roots with an octave-jump habit; funk bass on the disco material\", so the cell shapes carry the octave and a walking disco shape. Harmony is \"4-bar diatonic loops\" over \"bright majors with a IV—V—vi lift\", carried as the top family. The arrangement and melody blocks carry what the entry says is the group's actual parameter: \"nine voices distributed as short solo lines converging on a group hook\" and \"member lines are 2 bars each\", so `phraseBars` is 2-dominant, the structure is `call_response`, and the sections are choreography-locked at 8 bars with the title hook repeated as a post-chorus. The entry's \"dance-break\" is carried by the `bridge` slot in the second structure: engine/src/arrange.rs has no dance-break section kind and no rule strips a section to instruments, so a bridge is the closest available encoding rather than a literal one. \"Extremely hook-dense with an onomatopoeic or chanted title hook\" is the high `densityPerBar`; \"countermelody is a pitched instrumental riff\" is `answer_lick` first. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says \"tempo/harmony bands are genre-derived\": every drum probability, `swing.amount`, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 120 (the midpoint of the stated 105—135 band) are INFERRED; so is the `lydian` weight in `session.scales`, because the entry names \"bright majors\" and a late \"retro-synth minor\" and no mode at all, so lydian is an inferred bright-major colour at weight 2, and the entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the nine-voice distribution claim is repeated here.",
